delta_low: increase REGIONS and made cache for multi-language builds

When building an engine supporting multiple languages (such as Eloqium's 8
genuine language modules simultaneously linked into one shared library), each
language registers its stores and rule tables. The default REGIONS limit of
512 is exceeded during initialization of the 7th/8th language, causing an
abort() in delta_low_copy(). Furthermore, the lookup cache `made` of 16 entries
overflows.

Increasing REGIONS to 2048 and the `made` cache to 128 allows all 8 genuine
OpenEVV language modules to be initialized and executed without memory
exhaustion or abort().

diff --git a/src/delta/delta_low.c b/src/delta/delta_low.c
--- a/src/delta/delta_low.c
+++ b/src/delta/delta_low.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
    seventy-five and German ninety, plus two of dictionary entries apiece. A
    language is registered the first time one of its machines is made, so a
    program that never speaks the second one never spends its share. */
-#define REGIONS 512
+#define REGIONS 2048
 
 static struct {
     const unsigned char *at;
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ void *delta_low_copy(const void *what, size_t bytes)
     static struct {
         const void *what;
         void       *copy;
-    } made[16];
+    } made[128];
     static int mades;
 
     void *copy;
